From: jackie grey <leftstick22@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Apr 2026 00:28:11 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Add cabinet_bus plugin: socket bridge for the cabinet-bus
 server

A Lua plugin that opens a TCP listener on 127.0.0.1:5051 and accepts
newline-terminated JSON commands from the Arcade Cabinet Fault
Simulator's Flask cabinet-bus. This lets the browser UI control the
running emulator (pause / resume / soft reset / state query) alongside
the existing fault-injection on the standalone netlist.

Protocol is newline-delimited JSON in both directions. Supported
commands: ping, get_state, pause, resume, soft_reset. Replies always
carry an 'ok' boolean.

The plugin defaults to start='false' (per plugin.json) so it has no
effect unless explicitly enabled with -plugin cabinet_bus on the MAME
command line.

Co-Authored-By: Oz <oz-agent@warp.dev>
